N.C. Gen. Stat. § 1-52

(16) Personal injury or physical damage to plaintiff's property. — Within three years an action:

a. For bodily harm, or injury, falsely described;

b. For taking, detaining, or injuring personal property, including actions for the specific recovery of personal property;

c. For injury to the person or rights of another, not arising on contract and not hereinafter enumerated.
